statement:
Let $\mathbb{R}[x]$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients. Find all functions $f : \mathbb{R}[x] \to \mathbb{R}[x]$ satisfying the following conditions:
\begin{itemize}
\item $f$ maps the zero polynomial to itself;
\item for any non-zero polynomial $P \in \mathbb{R}[x]$, $\deg f(P) \leq 1 + \deg P$;
\item for any two polynomials $P, Q \in \mathbb{R}[x]$, the polynomials $P - f(Q)$ and $Q - f(P)$ have the same set of real roots.
\end{itemize}
